  "revisionPolicy": "Survey estimates are final on release. Each survey year is a cross-section; the five years (2017-18 to 2021-22) are comparable by design but are never chained into a spliced index.",
  "coverage": "All India; GER by social category × gender (SC, ST, All Categories — the API serves no OBC GER), GPI by social category, and enrolment by gender (Grand Total)",
  "note": "Survey years are fiscal (Apr–Mar), plotted at April of the first year. The five AISHE rounds served by the eSankhyiki API (2017-18 to 2021-22) are comparable by design but are never chained into a spliced index. GER (Gross Enrolment Ratio) = enrolled students ÷ the college-age population × 100; it is gross, so it can exceed 100. GPI (Gender Parity Index) = female GER ÷ male GER; 1.0 is parity. GER for SC and ST runs below the All-India ratio in every year; the gender gap within each group is what GPI measures. The AISHE API publishes GER only for SC, ST and All Categories — there is no OBC GER series to serve."
